{"title":"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine (with proof) whether there is a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of the integers with the following property: for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> there is exactly one solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f5e1443ba31f510d40088cdff6cd87931b561e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/52207175dcfbee037c7ce7b5d02df3053232828f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\in X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start with an incomplete subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42d8b2acfd33d2b1851a2ced0d8b82df581733e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = (S_1, S_2, S_3, ... S_m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"168\" height=\"18\" />, such that for any integer n, there is exactly zero or one solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f5e1443ba31f510d40088cdff6cd87931b561e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c735d6a627b91150d3ebdeae431fc2f86df26b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the smallest integer such that for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8ba1a488358f9496dab932ec5d35ccdddc65351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_i| &lt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d27a92289cf26bbceb54b04922452846986492bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_i+2S_j| &lt; 3N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/4/f2471034924050fbf1b59048c09d74454ea66634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\nSuppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the smallest non-negative integer without a solution in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> yet. Clearly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4bd583972bf9c71d12adb610c4a999253dc2b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le M \\le 3N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />. Generate <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8493c6ceb4d5bd0ccd54bcd1146eeeafde58cc30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01dda5bd2ddbcf7d81394d8ca52e5085bf4cd0a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bd2e39426284164bf7aea8963f16e2f86ae3dfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1} = -10N - M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/c/19c2b0c99f0ad8bc6f8820121e073e21ca295161.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+2} = 5N + M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />. Thus, we now have the solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/d/c6deb4a54314383e1fe21f629989b56562b84765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1}+2S_{m+2} = M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><i>Note: The values 10 and 5 can be replaced by any sufficiently large values such that the first is twice the second.</i>\n</p><p><br />\nNow, we must prove that the addition of these two terms to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> does not result in an integer n that has two solutions. Of course, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8500e37138ba1fb407efe481578d56d3720c7a82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1} + 2S_{m+2} = M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" /> which previously had no solutions. Furthermore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358fd9e56c8518ba40ce8244610a88c57cb14c2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1} + 2S_{m+2} = -15N - M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<dl><dd>For any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/5/465ccc195c2bca8698a9d80cddbd2d0550809bba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-12N - M &lt; S_{m+1}+2S_i &lt; -8N-M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"311\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/0074b46daacb23c06ca91d836fa7d245694bbefe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-21N - 2M &lt; S_i+2S_{m+1} &lt; -19N - 2M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"336\" height=\"16\" />.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4bd583972bf9c71d12adb610c4a999253dc2b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le M \\le 3N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />, we get that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13a5b0ebc425510604fb67e76fbbad65fdaee82e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-18N &lt; S_{m+1}+2S_i &lt; -8N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"225\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311821b27fc5f9c414b703c2c707aa2b41970eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-27N &lt; S_i+2S_{m+1} &lt; -19N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"234\" height=\"16\" /></dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<dl><dd>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d3733a553979c136b9764b51fd16c8e1f6155b02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3N + M &lt; S_{m+2}+2S_i &lt; 5N + M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"271\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49e007572c93a9072ac05de4f5f9385f24720beb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9N+2M &lt; S_i+2S_{m+2} &lt; 11N+2M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"298\" height=\"16\" />.</dd></dl>\n<dl><dd><dl><dd>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/b/c4bd583972bf9c71d12adb610c4a999253dc2b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\le M \\le 3N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"15\" />, we get that  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726e46c0bcb068475b1586b92cf98ca7fba6c336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3N &lt; S_{m+2}+2S_i &lt; 8N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/f/60f718327cd09c143d0515c47cf149b307c5fe0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9N &lt; S_i+2S_{m+2} &lt; 17N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"16\" />.</dd></dl></dd></dl>\n<p>Since all of these sums (other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />) are either greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afa589b0d34f7ece43bf3a642c908f9d683dbc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3N$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> or less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/39447c4253ff1c2537aa89f83df4da26e995e0e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3N$\" width=\"39\" height=\"12\" />, they are all sums that previously had no solutions. Furthermore, none of these sums are duplicated, as sums of different forms are contained in disjoint ranges of integers.\n</p><p>Thus, we have proved that we can generate a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> such that all non-negative integers n have a unique solution <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f5e1443ba31f510d40088cdff6cd87931b561e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor negative integers M that have no solutions in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> a similar proof holds, but instead generating the terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e57f01e3ab566691dd6b5af8f28d7ae169b93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1} = 10N - M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/8/d5853a12843d8f0add5ba2278eb46e7c26def3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+2} = -5N + M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor any integer M that currently has no solution in S, we can always add two terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/9/8493c6ceb4d5bd0ccd54bcd1146eeeafde58cc30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"42\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01dda5bd2ddbcf7d81394d8ca52e5085bf4cd0a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"16\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/0/8500e37138ba1fb407efe481578d56d3720c7a82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_{m+1} + 2S_{m+2} = M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"16\" /> that do not result in duplicated sums.\n</p><p>Thus, there does exist a subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> of the integers such that for any integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> there is exactly one solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/f/76f5e1443ba31f510d40088cdff6cd87931b561e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + 2b = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4bab3e1b4572969615be9cf2c3ea98e3ff135bb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b \\in X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO\" title=\"1996 USAMO\">1996 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1996\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1996_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1996 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.040 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 290/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1282/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9120/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.912      1 -total\n 56.22%    6.697      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 41.24%    4.913      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15093:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190043 and revision id 93981. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}